              <a href="/products/flavor/fruit" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Fruit</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Browse by Strength</h3>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <a href="/products/strength/light" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Mild</a>
              <a href="/products/strength/normal" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Regular</a>
              <a href="/products/strength/strong" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Strong</a>
              <a href="/products/strength/extra-strong" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Extra Strong</a>
              <a href="/products/strength/super-strong" class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-primary/10 transition">Super Strong</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <section style="margin-top: 48px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div style="margin-top: 16px;">
          <h3>Is VELO or ON! stronger?</h3>
          <p>VELO offers higher maximum strengths (up to 17 mg per pouch in some European markets), while ON! tops out at 8 mg. VELO also delivers a faster initial nicotine hit due to higher pouch moisture. ON! provides a gentler, more sustained release.</p>

          <h3>Are ON! pouches smaller than VELO?</h3>
          <p>Yes. ON! specialises in mini-format pouches that are among the smallest on the market -- roughly thumbnail-sized. VELO offers both slim and mini formats, but even VELO's mini is larger than an ON! mini.</p>

          <h3>Is ON! FDA approved?</h3>
          <p>The on! PLUS range received FDA marketing authorisation in the United States in 2025 -- the first nicotine pouch to achieve this. This does not directly apply to European sales but signals rigorous safety testing. VELO has not pursued FDA authorisation.</p>

          <h3>Which is cheaper, VELO or ON!?</h3>
          <p>Prices are similar in most European markets. VELO cans run EUR 3.50-5.50 and ON! cans EUR 3.00-5.00 for 20 pouches each. On a per-milligram basis, VELO often provides more total nicotine per can due to higher-strength options.</p>

          <h3>Can I switch between VELO and ON!?</h3>
          <p>Yes. Many users keep both brands on rotation -- VELO for flavour variety and intensity, ON! for discreet, lighter use. The main adjustment is pouch size and nicotine delivery speed.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <JsonLd items={[blogPostingJsonLd, faqJsonLd]} />
    </div>
          <p style="font-size: 13px; color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground)); margin-top: 32px; font-style: italic;">
          Disclaimer: This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice. Nicotine is an addictive substance. If you have health concerns about nicotine use, consult a qualified healthcare professional.
        </p>
</article>
</Shop>
